ILAng Build Fixes for Modern GCC (13.x)
==========================================

This patch fixes compilation errors when building ILAng with modern GCC versions.

Two bugs fixed:
1. Missing <cstdint> header in str_util.h
2. GCC -Werror=maybe-uninitialized in googletest

================================================================================
BUG #1: Missing <cstdint> in str_util.h
================================================================================

Root cause: str_util.h uses uint64_t but doesn't include <cstdint>
Modern GCC is stricter about requiring proper includes.

Error:
  src/util/str_util.cc:19:32: error: 'uint64_t' was not declared in this scope
  note: 'uint64_t' is defined in header '<cstdint>'; did you forget to '#include <cstdint>'?

Fix: Add #include <cstdint> to the header file

================================================================================
PATCH 1/2: Add missing <cstdint> include
================================================================================
File: ILAng/include/ilang/util/str_util.h
Line: 9-10

--- a/include/ilang/util/str_util.h
+++ b/include/ilang/util/str_util.h
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #ifndef ILANG_UTIL_STR_UTIL_H__
 #define ILANG_UTIL_STR_UTIL_H__

+#include <cstdint>
 #include <string>
 #include <vector>


================================================================================
BUG #2: GCC maybe-uninitialized warning in googletest
================================================================================

Root cause: GCC 13.x detects potential uninitialized use in gtest-death-test.cc
The code treats all warnings as errors (-Werror), causing build failure.

Error:
  gtest-death-test.cc:1224:24: error: 'dummy' may be used uninitialized [-Werror=maybe-uninitialized]

Fix Option 1: Disable the specific warning for this file
Fix Option 2: Initialize the variable
Fix Option 3: Disable -Werror for googletest (recommended)

================================================================================
PATCH 2A/2: Disable -Werror for googletest (RECOMMENDED)
================================================================================
File: ILAng/extern/googletest/CMakeLists.txt or ILAng/CMakeLists.txt
Add after project() or find_package(GTest):

if(TARGET gtest)
  target_compile_options(gtest PRIVATE -Wno-error=maybe-uninitialized)
endif()

================================================================================
PATCH 2B/2: Alternative - Add compiler flag to main CMakeLists.txt
================================================================================
File: ILAng/CMakeLists.txt
Add to compiler flags section:

# Disable specific warnings for external dependencies
if(CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "GNU|Clang")
  add_compile_options(-Wno-error=maybe-uninitialized)
endif()

================================================================================
APPLYING THE PATCHES
================================================================================

Method 1: Manual application
-----------------------------
cd ila/ILAng

# Fix 1: Add <cstdint> include
vi include/ilang/util/str_util.h
# Add "#include <cstdint>" after line 9

# Fix 2: Disable -Werror for googletest
vi CMakeLists.txt
# Add the compiler flag disable after project()

Method 2: Using patch command
-----------------------------
# Create individual patch files from this document
# Then apply with:
cd ila/ILAng
patch -p1 < ../ilang_str_util.patch
patch -p1 < ../ilang_cmake.patch

Method 3: CMake override
-----------------------------
cd ila/ILAng/build
cmake .. -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS="-Wno-error=maybe-uninitialized"
make -j$(nproc)

================================================================================
VERIFICATION
================================================================================

After applying patches:

cd ila/ILAng
rm -rf build
mkdir build && cd build
cmake ..
make -j$(nproc)

Expected result:
  - No compilation errors
  - libilang.a built successfully
  - All targets complete

