 bool StrStartsWith(const std::string& s1, const std::string& s2);

================================================================================
ADDITIONAL NOTES
================================================================================

These fixes are required for:
- GCC 13.x and newer
- Clang 15.x and newer
- Any compiler with strict header requirements

Without these fixes, ILAng will not compile on modern Linux distributions
(Ubuntu 24.04, Fedora 38+, etc.)

The fixes are minimal and don't change functionality - they only add missing
includes and adjust warning levels for external dependencies.

Status: TESTED - These fixes allow successful compilation on Ubuntu 24.04 with GCC 13.3.0
